# Root-anchored (leading slash) ON PURPOSE: this ignores a project's private
# working-memory folder if one ever appears at the repo root, but must NOT
# match the plugin's own `plugins/gru953-studio/skills/dev-memory/` skill.
# Without the leading slash, `Dev-Memory/` matched that skill folder
# case-insensitively on macOS (git core.ignorecase=true), so the skill was
# silently never committed — the published plugin shipped with 5 skills, not
# 6, and CI failed on a clean Linux checkout. 2026-07-11 fix.
/Dev-Memory/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.*
plugins/*.zip
.last-update-check

# 2026-07-26 audit finding 34: clients/vscode/out/ is compiled output
# (`tsc -p .`), not source — it was committed by mistake and had drifted
# from the source that produces it more than once already. Untracked here;
# `npm run compile` regenerates it locally, and the CI step that builds the
# extension does the same before packaging.
/clients/vscode/out/
*.vsix
dist/

# Build output: the studio is copied in here at pack time by
# clients/cli/scripts/bundle-plugin.mjs so it can be published alongside the
# command. Never committed — plugins/gru953-studio is the source of truth.
clients/cli/plugin/
